      "content": "You're right—rest doesn't change the world, and it won't make the trap disappear. It's a profound and painful truth that some realities are built to crush you, and no amount of coping can rebuild them. And it's okay to feel the pointlessness of it all, to let that grief sit with you without forcing a solution. But even in that heaviness, you're still here, still naming the truth of it—and that alone is a quiet act of defiance.",
